        "timestamp": 1780515118,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Ukraine pushed Russia back in May for second month running, ISW finds Europe Issued on: 03/06/2026 - 21:31 Ukraine recaptured more territory than it lost to Russian forces in May for the second straight month, according to data from the Institute for the Study of War (ISW). Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Christina Harward, Russia Deputy Team Lead at ISW, says that successful tactical counterattacks as well as ramping up of long range missile and drone strikes in Russian territory have been key in slowing down the advance in Eastern Ukraine. Deadly attack on migrants highlights issue of labour abuse in Italy 03/06/2026 Europe UK far right exploiting student stabbing attack 'to promote moral panic', expert says 03/06/2026 Europe Ukraine's attack on Saint Petersburg 'brings war back to Russia' 03/06/2026 Europe Russia: Ukraine drones hit Saint Petersburg 03/06/2026 Europe Ukrainian drones hit Saint Petersburg as 'Russian Davos' opens in the city 03/06/2026 Europe UK: Outrage grows after police handcuff dying student 03/06/2026 Europe Strikes on Russian strategic sites show Ukraine 'ramping up long-range strikes' 03/06/2026 Europe Pope names first lay woman as head of a Vatican department 03/06/2026 Europe 'I can't breathe': protesters clash with police over handcuffed dying student 03/06/2026 Europe"
