        "timestamp": 1780513463,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Deadly attack on migrants highlights issue of labour abuse in Italy Europe Issued on: 03/06/2026 - 21:04 Four migrants ​working as fruit pickers in slave-like conditions in southern Italy have been burned to death in a grisly murder case that is prompting fresh national soul-searching over labour exploitation. The migrants were found on Monday in ​a burned-out ‌van parked in a petrol station in Amendolara, in the southern region ⁠of Calabria. Surveillance cameras showed two people setting the car alight before running away. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome. UK far right exploiting student stabbing attack 'to promote moral panic', expert says 03/06/2026 Europe Ukraine's attack on Saint Petersburg 'brings war back to Russia' 03/06/2026 Europe Russia: Ukraine drones hit Saint Petersburg 03/06/2026 Europe Ukrainian drones hit Saint Petersburg as 'Russian Davos' opens in the city 03/06/2026 Europe UK: Outrage grows after police handcuff dying student 03/06/2026 Europe Strikes on Russian strategic sites show Ukraine 'ramping up long-range strikes' 03/06/2026 Europe Pope names first lay woman as head of a Vatican department 03/06/2026 Europe 'I can't breathe': protesters clash with police over handcuffed dying student 03/06/2026 Europe Frederiksen to remain Denmark's PM leading centre-left coalition government 03/06/2026 Europe"
